# Shell scripts must stay LF: a CRLF install.sh fails on the host with
#     /bin/sh^M: bad interpreter
# which names neither the file nor the cause.
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf

# Packages are BINARY, stated rather than sniffed.
#
# `* text=auto` above asks git to guess, and a 25 MB .deb that it ever guessed was text would
# be rewritten on checkout and then fail its own sha256 on the host -- loudly, but for a reason
# nobody would work out from the message. The packages are the whole point of this repository
# now, so nothing about them should be left to detection.
*.deb binary
*.rpm binary

# Signatures and checksums ARE text, and must stay LF. `sha256sum -c` compares the whole line,
# so one trailing CR makes a correct checksum fail.
*.asc    text eol=lf
*.sha256 text eol=lf
